    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-047. Marks the ADR as Implemented with the honest **zero-first-viewport-delta** caveat.\n\n## The delta (honest accounting)\n\n**Zero first-viewport delta.** Diagnostic with `HONEYBEE_LOG=paint` on the Wikipedia HTML article:\n\n```\nCascade elements with mask-image:  28  (all .vector-icon)\nLayout boxes with mask_has = true:  3\nPaint \"mask:\" log lines:            0\n```\n\nAll 3 layout-visible masks are inside `display:none` or `visibility:hidden` ancestors. ADR-032's culling short-circuits paint before reaching them. **Correct behavior, not a bug.**\n\nThe spec's predicted first-viewport target (`.cdx-message__icon`) doesn't exist in the fetched HTML — the issue box uses `.ambox` classes, not `.cdx-message`. Same phantom-target pattern as ADR-043's `mw-editsection`.\n\n## The fifth verification category\n\nADR-047 introduces a new category to the session's honest ledger:\n\n| Category | Example | Honest? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **PNG-verified (first-viewport)** | ADR-042 title underline, ADR-043 toolbar line | yes |\n| **PNG-verified (scroll)** | ADR-045 external link icons | yes |\n| **Behaviorally-complete, visually-subtle** | ADR-044 2px rounding | yes |\n| **Behaviorally-complete, visually-zero** | **ADR-047 mask infrastructure** | yes (documented) |\n| **Deferred with reason** | ADR-041 Commit 2, ADR-043 commits 2-3 | yes |\n\nThe zero-delta category is legitimate — the code is correct, tested, and ready. It just has no visible consumer today. Same \"parse for the future\" pattern as ADR-041 Commit 1.\n\n## Two bugs caught by unit tests before commit\n\n**1. Use-after-free (SIGSEGV)** — initial `mask_lookup` returned `const std::string*` pointing into a temporary `optional<string>`. First parse crashed. Fixed by returning `std::string` by value.\n\n**2. String-replace collision** — `for (char c : *ps)` → `for (char c : ps)` replacement hit `apply_inline_bg_pp`'s loop (ADR-045) instead of the mask block. Fixed by context-scoped replacement.\n\nBoth caught before commit. The tests did their job.\n\n## Why this cycle ships\n\n- **Paint code correct** (~90 lines, `cairo_mask` with inverse matrix)\n- **Layout-level test confirms** 3 boxes get `mask_has=true` with correct URL/size/position\n- **Paint-level diagnostic confirms** zero paint calls (correct — all culled)\n- **Zero regression surface**: every masked box is already invisible via ADR-032\n- **Future-ready**: the moment ADR-029 (header flex) lands, the 3 culled icons render with zero code change\n\n## Docs updated\n\n- ADR-047 → Implemented with zero-delta caveat\n- ADR-034: Post-ADR-047 note (three image subsystems)\n- ADR-045: Post-ADR-047 note (mask-image deferral closed)\n- README row 047\n- CHANGELOG entry with the diagnostic + honest framing\n\n## Test count\n\n- 598 cases / 2307 assertions all pass\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #224\n",
